From: glebn2 <40612835+glebn2@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] NotificationRecord: light notifications by default

Most apps never call enableLights(true), so the notification LED of
BALMUDA Phone hardly ever lit. Show the light for every channel unless the
user turned it off for that channel (USER_LOCKED_LIGHTS). Ongoing
notifications (USB debugging, USB, downloads) don't light it this way, or
the LED would stay on and hide the charging light. Devices without a
notification LED are not affected (canShowLightsLocked).
---
 .../android/server/notification/NotificationRecord.java    | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/notification/NotificationRecord.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/notification/NotificationRecord.java
index 44300dd..5becc82 100644
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/notification/NotificationRecord.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/notification/NotificationRecord.java
@@ -369,7 +369,12 @@ public final class NotificationRecord {
 
         int channelLightColor = getChannel().getLightColor() != 0 ? getChannel().getLightColor()
                 : defaultLightColor;
-        Light light = getChannel().shouldShowLights() ? new Light(channelLightColor,
+        // BALMUDA Phone: light every channel unless the user turned the light off;
+        // ongoing notifications don't light it
+        final boolean channelLights = getChannel().shouldShowLights()
+                || ((getChannel().getUserLockedFields() & NotificationChannel.USER_LOCKED_LIGHTS) == 0
+                        && (getSbn().getNotification().flags & Notification.FLAG_ONGOING_EVENT) == 0);
+        Light light = channelLights ? new Light(channelLightColor,
                 defaultLightOn, defaultLightOff) : null;
         if (mPreChannelsNotification
                 && (getChannel().getUserLockedFields()
